# ~/.ssh/config — LOCAL-ONLY, intentionally NOT managed by chezmoi.
#
# Why: work SSH tooling rewrites ~/.ssh/config on every run, re-inserting its
# own configuration block at the top of the file. Letting chezmoi manage this
# file would fight that tooling forever and leak the work configuration (host
# names, absolute paths) into this public repo. So ~/.ssh/config stays local
# and everything managed is pulled in through the Include below.
#
# Bootstrap on a new machine:
#
#   - Personal (non-work) machine: copy this file to ~/.ssh/config
#         cp ~/.ssh/config.example ~/.ssh/config
#
#   - Work machine: first run your work SSH tooling so it generates
#     ~/.ssh/config with its own block, then append the two lines at the bottom
#     of this file (Match all + Include) BELOW that work-managed block.
#
# IMPORTANT — the `Match all` before the Include is required. The work tooling
# writes its block as a host-specific `Host <work-hosts>` section, and an
# `Include` that sits inside a non-matching Host block is skipped entirely.
# Without this reset to global scope, the personal config under config.d/*
# would only apply when connecting to those work hosts. (Verified with
# `ssh -G`.)
#
# The work-managed block lands above these lines, e.g.:
#
#   Host <work-hosts>
#   Include /path/to/work_ssh_config

Match all
Include ~/.ssh/config.d/*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — pre-connect resource sync (glyph/gitmoji picker DB).
#
# The picker database (~/.local/share/fonts/nerd-font/symbols.db) is a
# host-specific artifact: it is built on THIS desktop/laptop and bakes in the
# renderability of this machine's terminal + font — which is exactly what
# draws the glyphs when you SSH into a headless dev-shell. So the remote copy
# must mirror whichever machine is connecting. This hook pushes it on every
# connection; rsync sends only the changed blocks and is a near-instant no-op
# when nothing changed.
#
# This is host-specific, so it stays in this LOCAL file only and never goes
# back to the repo. To enable: copy the line below, uncomment it, and replace
# BOTH <devbox> tokens with your dev-shell's Host alias. The remote
# ~/.local/share/fonts/nerd-font/ directory must already exist.
#
# Why each piece:
#   * `_DBSYNC` sentinel — rsync opens its own ssh to <devbox>, which re-reads
#     this config; the guard stops that second pass from re-running the hook
#     (otherwise: infinite loop). The `_DBSYNC=1 rsync` exports it into that
#     child ssh, which then sees it set and skips.
#   * `; false` — makes this a side-effect-only block that contributes no SSH
#     config (the exec never "matches").
#   * timeouts + </dev/null — a sleeping/unreachable dev-shell can't stall or
#     swallow stdin from your login; worst case you connect with a stale copy.
#
# Match host <devbox> exec "[ -n \"$_DBSYNC\" ] || _DBSYNC=1 rsync -z --timeout=8 -e 'ssh -o ConnectTimeout=5' ~/.local/share/fonts/nerd-font/symbols.db <devbox>:.local/share/fonts/nerd-font/ </dev/null >/dev/null 2>&1; false"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
